==German==

===Etymology 1===
Probably a [[pars pro toto]] expression, from a very old root (related to Ancient Greek {{term|φαλλός||penis|tr=phallos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}), with the related meaning "ball".

====Noun====
{{de-noun-m|genitive=Bullen|plural=Bullen}}

# a [[bull]] (male cow)

===Etymology 2===
From ''(Land)Puller'', a non-derogative term for a policeman of the 18. century. In the 1960s, the term ''Bullen'' was first used by left protesters, possibly associating the American derogative term ''[[pig]]'' of that time to the animal ''[[bull]]''.

====Noun====
{{de-noun-m|genitive=Bullen|plural=Bullen}}

# (derogative) a male [[cop]]

=====Related terms=====
* [[Bullette]]

===Etymology 3===
From {{etyl|la}} ''[[bulla]]'' "seal capsule", originally meaning "ball, bullet".

====Noun====
'''Bulle''' ''f''

# a [[bulla]] (papal decree)

=====Related terms=====
* [[Bulette]]

